1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,002
This is MuleTrace, a risk,

2
00:00:01,964 --> 00:00:06,065
fraud and regulatory intelligence copilot for banks and NBFCs.

3
00:00:06,679 --> 00:00:10,178
It finds mule-account networks hidden in transaction data,

4
00:00:10,184 --> 00:00:12,912
explains each one with evidence and policy,

5
00:00:12,874 --> 00:00:16,137
and drafts an audit-ready suspicious transaction report.

6
00:00:16,690 --> 00:00:18,068
Here is the problem.

7
00:00:18,705 --> 00:00:22,582
Ten lakh rupees can leave a bank as two thousand transfers of five

8
00:00:22,444 --> 00:00:24,870
hundred rupees, through a hundred mule accounts.

9
00:00:25,490 --> 00:00:29,513
Every transfer sits below every threshold, so no rule fires.

10
00:00:30,122 --> 00:00:32,571
The fraud is only visible as a network.

11
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:35,212
Here is the end-to-end workflow,

12
00:00:35,274 --> 00:00:39,442
executed live in Snowflake's CoCo CLI with three modular skills.

13
00:00:40,057 --> 00:00:43,611
Input: the ingest skill verifies what landed in Snowflake:

14
00:00:43,628 --> 00:00:47,573
ten thousand transactions, six hundred accounts with KYC data,

15
00:00:47,568 --> 00:00:49,470
and seventeen policy sections,

16
00:00:49,487 --> 00:00:51,959
our structured and unstructured sources.

17
00:00:52,579 --> 00:00:55,865
Processing: the detect skill calls our Snowpark procedure,

18
00:00:55,894 --> 00:00:59,303
which runs the graph detector inside Snowflake and ranks six

19
00:00:59,164 --> 00:01:00,329
laundering networks,

20
00:01:00,302 --> 00:01:03,611
led by a ₹9.94 lakh structuring ring.

21
00:01:04,242 --> 00:01:04,972
Output:

22
00:01:05,023 --> 00:01:08,566
the investigate skill pulls the evidence pack and the policy clause

23
00:01:08,427 --> 00:01:10,675
it breaches, records an escalation,

24
00:01:10,648 --> 00:01:14,861
and calls Cortex AI to draft the grounds of suspicion for the STR.

25
00:01:14,733 --> 00:01:18,756
Model thinking time is sped up; every query and result is real.

26
00:01:25,310 --> 00:01:28,764
This is the investigator workspace, live on Cloudflare.

27
00:01:29,378 --> 00:01:33,111
The header shows the month at a glance: transactions, accounts,

28
00:01:33,073 --> 00:01:36,080
networks found, and thirty lakh rupees at risk.

29
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:39,573
On the left is the alert queue, ranked by risk,

30
00:01:39,535 --> 00:01:41,258
with a filter by typology.

31
00:01:41,878 --> 00:01:45,935
The canvas draws every network the detector found: a structuring ring,

32
00:01:45,907 --> 00:01:49,919
two layering chains, a fan-out and fan-in, and two round-trip cycles.

33
00:01:50,470 --> 00:01:53,566
Let's open the top alert, F001.

34
00:01:54,192 --> 00:01:57,970
A hundred accounts sent two thousand small transfers to one collector,

35
00:01:57,998 --> 00:02:01,095
eighty-four percent of them exactly five hundred rupees.

36
00:02:01,737 --> 00:02:05,682
The risk score of ninety-eight is fully explainable: pattern detected,

37
00:02:05,688 --> 00:02:09,566
amount at stake, account red flags, and pattern strength.

38
00:02:10,186 --> 00:02:15,670
Below it is the exact clause the network breaches, AML-04 section 3.2,

39
00:02:15,632 --> 00:02:17,423
quoted with its source document,

40
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:20,481
followed by every account and every transaction,

41
00:02:20,498 --> 00:02:23,338
exportable as a CSV evidence pack.

42
00:02:23,890 --> 00:02:26,161
Clicking an account opens its profile.

43
00:02:26,775 --> 00:02:30,519
This collector was opened just thirty-one days before the activity,

44
00:02:30,492 --> 00:02:32,026
holds minimum KYC,

45
00:02:31,987 --> 00:02:35,441
and received sixty-three times its declared monthly income.

46
00:02:36,072 --> 00:02:37,840
Its counterparties are listed,

47
00:02:37,836 --> 00:02:40,006
and the graph highlights its neighbourhood.

48
00:02:40,626 --> 00:02:41,992
Names stay masked,

49
00:02:41,987 --> 00:02:45,631
because an investigator doesn't need personal data to triage.

50
00:02:46,180 --> 00:02:49,176
The same evidence exists for every typology.

51
00:02:49,791 --> 00:02:52,474
F005 is a fan-out and fan-in:

52
00:02:52,436 --> 00:02:55,086
one source splits money across thirty mules,

53
00:02:55,092 --> 00:02:57,206
just under ten thousand rupees each,

54
00:02:57,179 --> 00:03:00,811
and they pass ninety-nine percent of it to one collector within hours.

55
00:03:01,443 --> 00:03:03,724
F002 is a layering chain:

56
00:03:03,775 --> 00:03:07,798
seven and a half lakh rupees hop through six accounts in twelve hours.

57
00:03:08,440 --> 00:03:10,778
F003 is a round trip:

58
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:13,802
money loops through four accounts and comes back home.

59
00:03:14,350 --> 00:03:15,583
Now the copilot.

60
00:03:16,208 --> 00:03:17,675
Ask in plain English:

61
00:03:17,659 --> 00:03:21,470
which accounts received over five lakh rupees in transfers under a

62
00:03:21,331 --> 00:03:22,062
thousand?

63
00:03:22,682 --> 00:03:25,175
It finds the collector, links the finding,

64
00:03:25,148 --> 00:03:26,972
and quotes the policy clause.

65
00:03:27,592 --> 00:03:29,115
Ask it to trace money,

66
00:03:29,099 --> 00:03:32,597
and it follows the funds from the fan-out source through thirty mules

67
00:03:32,459 --> 00:03:34,684
to one account within forty-eight hours.

68
00:03:35,304 --> 00:03:39,137
Ask a regulatory question, and it answers from the policy text:

69
00:03:39,177 --> 00:03:42,675
an STR is due to FIU-IND within seven working days.

70
00:03:43,296 --> 00:03:45,365
Every answer lists its sources.

71
00:03:45,920 --> 00:03:48,626
Every alert ends in a documented decision.

72
00:03:49,241 --> 00:03:53,141
The investigator adds a note and escalates to the Principal Officer.

73
00:03:53,761 --> 00:03:57,036
Switching the role to Principal Officer unmasks names,

74
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:59,614
just as a Snowflake masking policy would.

75
00:04:00,234 --> 00:04:04,134
One click drafts the suspicious transaction report: subjects,

76
00:04:04,084 --> 00:04:08,754
transactions, grounds of suspicion, policy basis, recommended actions,

77
00:04:08,749 --> 00:04:10,183
and the filing deadline.

78
00:04:10,803 --> 00:04:13,431
Only the Principal Officer can mark it filed,

79
00:04:13,392 --> 00:04:15,786
and every step lands in the audit log.

80
00:04:16,340 --> 00:04:18,220
All of this runs on Snowflake.

81
00:04:18,846 --> 00:04:22,511
Transactions and policy documents land in Snowflake tables.

82
00:04:23,132 --> 00:04:25,849
Dynamic Tables keep flow features fresh.

83
00:04:26,469 --> 00:04:30,480
The same Python detector runs as a Snowpark procedure on an hourly

84
00:04:30,341 --> 00:04:30,982
task.

85
00:04:31,603 --> 00:04:33,840
Cortex Search indexes the policies,

86
00:04:33,879 --> 00:04:37,076
a Cortex Agent combines a semantic view with search,

87
00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:39,610
so answers carry numbers and citations,

88
00:04:39,582 --> 00:04:42,322
and AI_COMPLETE drafts the report.

89
00:04:42,870 --> 00:04:45,598
The results: every planted scheme caught,

90
00:04:45,593 --> 00:04:49,404
no legitimate look-alikes flagged, and a complete path from signal,

91
00:04:49,399 --> 00:04:51,469
to evidence, to a filed report.

92
00:04:52,020 --> 00:04:53,007
MuleTrace.

93
00:04:53,622 --> 00:04:56,238
Follow the money, and file with confidence.
